-\section{Discussion}
-These systems learn executable local modules within a supplied interpreter.
-Native all-pass packages demonstrate finite functional learnability, not
-identification of each teacher's entire algorithm. BE is informative because
-native agreement leaves continuation behavior underconstrained. The budget,
-overlap and shared-head audits limit its interpretation to the measured
-procedures, with posthoc evidence on some unseen local input types.
-
-\paragraph{Safety and progress.}
-Exact availability and equal-offer rejection preserve partial properness.
-An always-wait policy is safe forever. On a $K$-clique, all nodes proposing
-one color with independent participation $1/2$ progress with probability
-$K/2^K$ per round. Diffuse independent proposals permit progress bounds,
-but those uniform hypotheses are not established for these checkpoints.
-MAX can implement a presence predicate and a finite-type COMMIT certificate
-(Appendix~\ref{app:math}); it does not establish candidate diversity,
-termination or palette-context invariance. All 45 selected canonical
-transfer cores fail the sufficient all-types condition, despite successful
-rollouts; five different historical E1 weights pass conditional certificates.
-These cohorts cannot be conflated. Vertex equivariance assumes consistent
-relabeling of observations, IDs and schedules in real arithmetic; ordered
-color features do not imply color-name equivariance.
-
-\paragraph{Output laws and limitations.}
-Properness and one-node marginals do not determine joint coloring laws.
-Historical studies use complete vectors/statuses, run-level permutations,
-fixed graph/checkpoint blocks and explicit testing families. They are
-supporting evidence, separate from the 810,000 runs
-(Appendix~\ref{app:laws}). Nonrejection is never equality; coupling and
-symmetry justify only stated bounds or special cases.
-Native cohorts differ in observations, supervision and budgets; combined
-coverage cannot rank architectures fairly. CF uses more labels, development
-states and familiar query templates. Shared heads limit independent
-architecture evidence. Pilot-selected conditions and paired graph/tape reuse
-limit extrapolation. Degree, palette and private-input scale are confounded.
-Failure witnesses do not settle every capacity/optimization cause.
-Teacher proofs use ideal randomness; hardware arithmetic and finite PRNGs
-need separate assumptions. Forty original Pedro weights remain unavailable;
-their historical traces are background, not a fully replayed or imputed cohort.
-
-We freeze scope. A label-matched CF comparison with new final states, held-out
-intervention families and paired seeds would address a stronger causal claim,
-not a prerequisite for the procedure comparison here. Multigrade retraining,
-general BE, asynchrony and architecture search remain future work.
